by nicolas-grekas at 2026-07-30T13:58:46Z

Psalm surfaced a second one of the same kind once the first cleared: `Couchbase\Collection` also does not exist without the extension. It has stubs for `\Redis`, `\Memcached` and `\PDO`, but not for those two PECL classes.

Both are now matched by class prefix, so this method names no class that might be missing:

```php
// Relay and Couchbase are matched by class prefix so that this file never names a
// class from an extension that might not be installed
$class = \is_object($connection) ? $connection::class : '';

return match (true) {
    $connection instanceof \Memcached => new MemcachedAdapter(...),
    $connection instanceof \PDO, \is_string($connection) && preg_match('/^(mysql|oci|pgsql|sqlsrv|sqlite):/', $connection) => new PdoAdapter(...),
    $connection instanceof \Redis, $connection instanceof \RedisArray, $connection instanceof \RedisCluster,
    $connection instanceof \Predis\ClientInterface,
    str_starts_with($class, 'Relay\\') => new RedisAdapter(...),
    str_starts_with($class, 'Couchbase\\') => new CouchbaseCollectionAdapter(...),
    default => throw new InvalidArgumentException(\sprintf('Unsupported connection: "%s".', get_debug_type($connection))),
};
```

The alternative was two entries in the Psalm baseline, which is how `RedisTrait` gets away with `instanceof Relay` today. I preferred not to grow the baseline for new code, but say so if you would rather see `instanceof` and accept the baseline entries.

